From 60f94b6950e4f852f48d8ff0433c01e0176a3688 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:04:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 079/274] TileLang V4.1 collectives: a rank-order all-reduce of
 any size

The rank-order reduce-scatter of the rows (zero-padded to a multiple of the
world size) followed by an all-gather, which only moves bits: every row is
the FP32 rank-order sum with one rounding that sparknet's one-shot all-reduce
computes, whatever the message size.

(cherry picked from commit 95fa3ac658ccaf22a630ec30bf727b433788f3fc)

diff --git a/tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_collectives.py b/tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_collectives.py
